WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:02.950
- [Narrator] This fuzzy
little creature is a quokka.

00:00:02.950 --> 00:00:05.340
And these guys live
here off the west coast

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:08.290
of Australia on Rottnest Island.

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:11.310
Quokkas are not only cute,
they are camera ready.

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:13.523
And they're taking the internet by storm.

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:20.820
So, let's start at the beginning.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.240
What is a quokka?

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:24.370
- A quokka is a small wallaby.

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:26.420
It comes from the same
family as a kangaroo.

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:28.770
And physically they've
got thick brown fur,

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:31.970
they've got long tails
and they hop around.

00:00:31.970 --> 00:00:33.520
Quokkas thrive on Rottnest Island

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:35.320
because they don't have
any predators over here,

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:36.780
so there's no foxes.

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:40.230
We have the largest viable
population of about 10,000.

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:41.800
- [Narrator] Oh, sorry, and you are?

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:44.240
- My name's Cassyanna Gray,
and I'm a conservation officer

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:45.420
on Rottnest Island.

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:46.840
In my role I'm responsible

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:48.723
for managing conservation programs.

00:00:48.723 --> 00:00:50.430
- [Narrator] And there's one online trend

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:52.550
that has really helped these animals.

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:53.860
A quokka selfie.

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:56.410
But make sure you're getting it right.

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:58.920
How to take a quokka selfie.

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:00.563
Step one: a camera.

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:03.863
Step two: a quokka.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:06.600
- But don't touch the quokkas.

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:08.250
- [Narrator] Ah, no.

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:09.100
- Or feed them.

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:11.000
It's $150 fine.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:12.332
- [Narrator] These guys
don't need the food.

00:01:12.332 --> 00:01:14.220
They naturally graze their way through

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:15.730
the island's vegetation.

00:01:15.730 --> 00:01:18.470
- And they also really love
the seedlings that we plant

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:20.900
as part of our re-vegetation projects

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:23.950
that we have implemented by
our environment technicians.

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:24.975
- [Narrator] Sorry about that guys.

00:01:24.975 --> 00:01:26.743
Thanks for all your hard work.

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:31.170
And what makes these guys
so great for taking selfies?

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:32.930
- [Cassyanna] Around the
settlement areas the quokkas

00:01:32.930 --> 00:01:35.050
are a lot friendlier; they've
become used to people,

00:01:35.050 --> 00:01:37.000
so their natural behaviors change.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:38.545
But out in the reserve
where they're actually still

00:01:38.545 --> 00:01:40.550
exhibiting their natural behavior,

00:01:40.550 --> 00:01:43.150
they will be a lot more wary of people.

00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:44.090
- [Narrator] We have to know,

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:46.540
are they actually smiling in photos?

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:47.730
- [Cassyanna] Yeah, they're
not actually smiling

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:49.980
in the photos, it's just the
natural shape of their mouth,

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:51.080
which comes up at the side,

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:53.506
which makes them look
like they're smiling.

00:01:53.506 --> 00:01:56.185
The popularity of the quokka selfie

00:01:56.185 --> 00:01:59.350
has given us the opportunity
to be able to raise awareness

00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:01.630
about the quokka's
particularly on the mainland

00:02:01.630 --> 00:02:03.070
that are under threat.

00:02:03.070 --> 00:02:06.280
So we use that as a platform
to educate the public

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:08.090
and also educate them about appropriate

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:09.760
interaction with wildlife.

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:13.100
- [Narrator] So finally,
a good cause for selfies.

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:15.683
(upbeat music)

